/-!
# Coinvariants and first continuous cohomology of the profinite integers

Let `M` be a topological abelian group with a continuous action of the profinite integers `zHat`.
This file computes the first continuous cohomology `H¹(zHat, M)` in terms of the endomorphism
`zHat.genSubId M : m ↦ zHat.gen • m - m` and its cokernel `M ⧸ (zHat.gen - 1) M`, supplying the
cohomological input needed downstream to compute unramified Galois cohomology `H¹_ur(K, M)` of
nonarchimedean local fields via Frobenius coinvariants and to establish the Frobenius order formula
`#H¹_ur(K, M) = #H⁰(G_K, M)`.

Evaluating a continuous `1`-cocycle `f : zHat → M` at the topological generator `zHat.gen` sends
the coboundary `g ↦ g • m - m` to `zHat.gen • m - m`, so it descends to a homomorphism

```text
zHat.evalGen M : H¹(zHat, M) →+ M ⧸ (zHat.gen - 1) M.
```

When `M` is `T₁`, the stabilizer of an element and the equalizer of two continuous `1`-cocycles
are closed subgroups containing the dense subgroup generated by `zHat.gen`. Consequently
`ker (zHat.gen - 1) = H⁰(zHat, M)` (`TauCeti.zHat.ker_genSubId_eq_fixedPoints`) and `zHat.evalGen M`
is injective (`TauCeti.zHat.evalGen_injective`).

For a general continuous `zHat`-module `M`, the quotient `M ⧸ (zHat.gen - 1) M` need not equal the
`zHat`-coinvariants, because `zHat.gen` only generates `zHat` topologically. When `M` is discrete
with a continuous `zHat`-action, every element is fixed by some congruence subgroup
`modSubgroup d` (`TauCeti.zHat.exists_modSubgroup_smul_eq_self`), so every `g • m - m` lies in the
range of `zHat.gen - 1` (`TauCeti.zHat.range_genSubId_eq_closure_smul_sub`), and the quotient
`TauCeti.zHat.Coinvariants M = M ⧸ (zHat.gen - 1) M` is genuinely the `zHat`-coinvariants of `M`.

For discrete `M`, surjectivity of `evalGen` requires an additional torsion hypothesis: for `ℤ` with
the trivial action, `H¹(zHat, ℤ)` is the group of continuous homomorphisms `zHat → ℤ`, which
vanishes by compactness of `zHat`, whereas `ℤ ⧸ (zHat.gen - 1) ℤ = ℤ`. When `M` is discrete and
torsion (`IsAddTorsion M`), every `m ∈ M` has an open stabilizer in `zHat` and finite additive
order, so the geometric-sum formula along a finite cyclic quotient `ZMod k` of `zHat` constructs a
continuous `1`-cocycle taking the value `m` at `zHat.gen`
(`TauCeti.zHat.exists_apply_gen_eq_of_isOfFinAddOrder`). Thus `zHat.evalGen M` is an isomorphism
`H¹(zHat, M) ≃+ zHat.Coinvariants M` (`TauCeti.zHat.h1AddEquivCoinvariants`). For compact totally
disconnected, finitely generated integral and finite-dimensional rational coefficients, `evalGen`
is surjective with no torsion hypothesis (`TauCeti.zHat.evalGen_surjective_of_profinite` and its
siblings in `TauCeti.Topology.Algebra.Group.Profinite.ZHat.Coinvariants.Profinite`). In general,
for `T₁` coefficients on which `evalGen` is surjective, it is an isomorphism
(`TauCeti.zHat.h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective`).

For a finite `T₁` (hence discrete) `zHat`-module `M`, comparing the kernel and cokernel of the
endomorphism `zHat.gen - 1` yields `#H¹(zHat, M) = #H⁰(zHat, M)`
(`TauCeti.zHat.natCard_H1_eq_natCard_H0`).

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.zHat.genSubId`: the endomorphism `m ↦ zHat.gen • m - m` of a `zHat`-module `M`.
* `TauCeti.zHat.evalGen`: evaluation at `zHat.gen`, `H¹(zHat, M) →+ M ⧸ (zHat.genSubId M).range`.
* `TauCeti.zHat.h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective`: the isomorphism
  `H¹(zHat, M) ≃+ M ⧸ (zHat.genSubId M).range` for `T₁` `M` on which `evalGen` is surjective.
* `TauCeti.zHat.Coinvariants`: the `zHat`-coinvariants `M ⧸ (zHat.genSubId M).range` of a discrete
  continuous `zHat`-module `M`.
* `TauCeti.zHat.h1AddEquivCoinvariants`: the isomorphism `H¹(zHat, M) ≃+ zHat.Coinvariants M` for a
  discrete torsion `zHat`-module `M`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.zHat.ker_genSubId_eq_fixedPoints`: for `T₁` `M`, `ker(zHat.gen - 1) = M^{zHat}`.
* `TauCeti.zHat.cocycles_ext_of_apply_gen`, `TauCeti.zHat.evalGen_injective`: for `T₁` `M`, a
  continuous `1`-cocycle is determined by its value at `zHat.gen`, and `evalGen` is injective.
* `TauCeti.zHat.exists_modSubgroup_smul_eq_self`, `TauCeti.zHat.range_genSubId_eq_closure_smul_sub`:
  for discrete `M`, every element is fixed by some `modSubgroup d`, and `(zHat.gen - 1) M` equals
  the `zHat`-augmentation subgroup generated by all `g • m - m`.
* `TauCeti.zHat.evalGen_surjective_of_forall_exists`: `evalGen` is surjective when every element is
  the value at `zHat.gen` of a continuous `1`-cocycle.
* `TauCeti.zHat.exists_apply_gen_eq_of_isOfFinAddOrder`, `TauCeti.zHat.evalGen_surjective`: for
  discrete torsion `M`, every element is the value at `zHat.gen` of a continuous `1`-cocycle.
* `TauCeti.zHat.natCard_coinvariants_eq_natCard_H0`, `TauCeti.zHat.natCard_H1_eq_natCard_H0`: for a
  finite discrete `zHat`-module `M`, `#H¹(zHat, M) = #H⁰(zHat, M)`.
* `TauCeti.zHat.subsingleton_H1_of_subsingleton_H0`: a finite discrete `zHat`-module with trivial
  invariants has vanishing `H¹`.

## References

* [J.-P. Serre, *Corps Locaux*][serre1968], Chapter XIII, §1, Proposition 1.
* J.-P. Serre, *Galois Cohomology*, Springer, 1997, Chapter I, §2.2, Exercise 2.
* J. Neukirch, A. Schmidt, K. Wingberg, *Cohomology of Number Fields*, 2nd ed., Proposition 1.7.7.
* J. S. Milne, *Arithmetic Duality Theorems*, 2nd ed., Chapter I, Lemma 2.7.
-/

public noncomputable section

namespace TauCeti.zHat

open ContCohomology groupCohomology
open scoped IsMulCommutative

universe u v

section GenSubId

variable (M : Type v) [AddCommGroup M] [DistribMulAction zHat.{u} M]

/-- **The endomorphism `zHat.gen - 1`** on an additive group `M` with a distributive action of
`zHat`, sending `m` to `zHat.gen • m - m`. -/
def genSubId : M →+ M where
  toFun m := gen • m - m
  map_zero' := by rw [smul_zero, sub_self]
  map_add' a b := by
    rw [smul_add]
    abel

/-- `genSubId` sends `m` to `zHat.gen • m - m`. -/
@[simp]
theorem genSubId_apply (m : M) : genSubId.{u} M m = gen • m - m :=
  (rfl)

section T1

variable [TopologicalSpace M] [T1Space M] [ContinuousSMul zHat.{u} M]

/-- **An element of a `T₁` continuous `zHat`-module fixed by `zHat.gen` is fixed by `zHat`**, since
the stabilizer of an element is closed and contains the dense subgroup generated by `zHat.gen`. -/
theorem ker_genSubId_eq_fixedPoints :
    (genSubId.{u} M).ker = FixedPoints.addSubgroup zHat.{u} M := by
  ext m
  rw [AddMonoidHom.mem_ker, genSubId_apply, sub_eq_zero, FixedPoints.mem_addSubgroup]
  refine ⟨fun hm g ↦ ?_, fun hm ↦ hm gen⟩
  have htop : (⊤ : Subgroup zHat.{u}) ≤ MulAction.stabilizer zHat.{u} m := by
    rw [← topologicalClosure_zpowers_gen.{u}, ← closedZpowers_def]
    exact (closedZpowers_le (isClosed_stabilizer (continuous_id.smul continuous_const))).mpr hm
  exact MulAction.mem_stabilizer_iff.mp (htop (Subgroup.mem_top g))

/-- **For a finite `T₁` (hence discrete) continuous `zHat`-module, the coinvariants and invariants
have the same order**, as the cokernel and kernel of the endomorphism `genSubId M`. -/
theorem natCard_coinvariants_eq_natCard_H0 [Finite M] :
    Nat.card (M ⧸ (genSubId.{u} M).range) = Nat.card (H0 zHat.{u} M) := by
  rw [← AddSubgroup.index_eq_card, AddSubgroup.index_range, ker_genSubId_eq_fixedPoints]

end T1

end GenSubId

section Evaluation

variable (M : Type v) [AddCommGroup M] [TopologicalSpace M] [IsTopologicalAddGroup M]
  [DistribMulAction zHat.{u} M]

/-- Evaluating a continuous `1`-cocycle at `zHat.gen`, composed with the quotient map to
`M ⧸ (genSubId M).range`. -/
private def evalGenZ1 : Z1 zHat.{u} M →+ M ⧸ (genSubId.{u} M).range :=
  (QuotientAddGroup.mk' (genSubId.{u} M).range).comp
    { toFun f := f.val gen
      map_zero' := rfl
      map_add' _ _ := rfl }

private theorem B1_le_ker_evalGenZ1 :
    (B1 zHat.{u} M).addSubgroupOf (Z1 zHat.{u} M) ≤ (evalGenZ1.{u} M).ker := by
  intro f hf
  rw [AddSubgroup.mem_addSubgroupOf, mem_B1_iff] at hf
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hf
  rw [AddMonoidHom.mem_ker, evalGenZ1, AddMonoidHom.comp_apply, QuotientAddGroup.mk'_apply,
    QuotientAddGroup.eq_zero_iff]
  exact ⟨m, hm gen⟩

variable [ContinuousSMul zHat.{u} M]

/-- **Evaluation at the topological generator `zHat.gen`**, inducing a homomorphism
`H¹(zHat, M) →+ M ⧸ (zHat.gen - 1) M`. -/
def evalGen : H1 zHat.{u} M →+ M ⧸ (genSubId.{u} M).range :=
  QuotientAddGroup.lift ((B1 zHat.{u} M).addSubgroupOf (Z1 zHat.{u} M))
    (evalGenZ1.{u} M) (B1_le_ker_evalGenZ1 M)

/-- On the class of a continuous `1`-cocycle `f`, `evalGen` is the coset of `f gen` modulo
`(genSubId M).range`. -/
@[simp]
theorem evalGen_mk (f : Z1 zHat.{u} M) :
    evalGen.{u} M (f : H1 zHat.{u} M) = QuotientAddGroup.mk (f.val gen) :=
  (rfl)

variable {M} in
/-- **Evaluation at `zHat.gen` is surjective on `H¹(zHat, M)`** as soon as every element of `M` is
the value at `zHat.gen` of a continuous `1`-cocycle. -/
theorem evalGen_surjective_of_forall_exists (h : ∀ m : M, ∃ f : Z1 zHat.{u} M, f.val gen = m) :
    Function.Surjective (evalGen.{u} M) := by
  intro q
  induction q using QuotientAddGroup.induction_on with
  | _ m =>
    obtain ⟨f, hf⟩ := h m
    exact ⟨f, by rw [evalGen_mk, hf]⟩

section Injectivity

variable {M} [T1Space M]

omit [ContinuousSMul zHat.{u} M] in
/-- **Two continuous `1`-cocycles on `zHat` with values in a `T₁` module that agree at `zHat.gen`
are equal**, because `{zHat.gen}` topologically generates `zHat`. -/
theorem cocycles_ext_of_apply_gen {f g : Z1 zHat.{u} M} (h : f.val gen = g.val gen) :
    f = g :=
  Subtype.ext <| eq_of_mem_Z1_of_eqOn_of_topologicalClosure_closure_eq_top f.property g.property
    topologicalClosure_closure_gen.{u} (fun _ hx ↦ (Set.mem_singleton_iff.mp hx) ▸ h)

variable (M) in
/-- **Evaluation at `zHat.gen` is injective on `H¹(zHat, M)`** for every `T₁` continuous
`zHat`-module `M`. -/
theorem evalGen_injective : Function.Injective (evalGen.{u} M) := by
  rw [← AddMonoidHom.ker_eq_bot_iff, eq_bot_iff]
  intro x hx
  induction x using QuotientAddGroup.induction_on with
  | _ f =>
    rw [AddMonoidHom.mem_ker, evalGen_mk, QuotientAddGroup.eq_zero_iff] at hx
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hx
    rw [AddSubgroup.mem_bot, H1pi_eq_zero_iff, mem_B1_iff]
    let b : Z1 zHat.{u} M := ⟨d0 zHat.{u} M m, B1_le_Z1 zHat.{u} M (d0_mem_B1 m)⟩
    have hfb : f = b := cocycles_ext_of_apply_gen
      (hm.symm.trans ((genSubId_apply M m).trans (d0_apply m gen).symm))
    exact ⟨m, fun g ↦ (d0_apply m g).symm.trans (congrFun (congrArg Subtype.val hfb) g).symm⟩

/-- For a `T₁` continuous `zHat`-module `M`, a class in `H¹(zHat, M)` vanishes if and only if its
image under `evalGen M` vanishes. -/
@[simp]
theorem evalGen_eq_zero_iff {x : H1 zHat.{u} M} : evalGen.{u} M x = 0 ↔ x = 0 :=
  map_eq_zero_iff (evalGen.{u} M) (evalGen_injective M)

/-- **`H¹(zHat, M) ≃+ M ⧸ (zHat.gen - 1) M` via evaluation at `zHat.gen`** for a `T₁` continuous
`zHat`-module `M` on which `evalGen` is surjective. -/
def h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective (h : Function.Surjective (evalGen.{u} M)) :
    H1 zHat.{u} M ≃+ M ⧸ (genSubId.{u} M).range :=
  AddEquiv.ofBijective (evalGen.{u} M) ⟨evalGen_injective M, h⟩

/-- `h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective` acts as `evalGen`. -/
@[simp]
theorem h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective_apply (h : Function.Surjective (evalGen.{u} M))
    (x : H1 zHat.{u} M) : h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective h x = evalGen.{u} M x :=
  (rfl)

/-- The underlying additive homomorphism of `h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective` is `evalGen`. -/
@[simp]
theorem h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective_toAddMonoidHom
    (h : Function.Surjective (evalGen.{u} M)) :
    (h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective h : H1 zHat.{u} M →+ M ⧸ (genSubId.{u} M).range) =
      evalGen.{u} M :=
  (rfl)

/-- Evaluating at `zHat.gen` cancels the inverse of `h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective`. -/
@[simp]
theorem evalGen_h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective_symm (h : Function.Surjective (evalGen.{u} M))
    (q : M ⧸ (genSubId.{u} M).range) :
    evalGen.{u} M ((h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective h).symm q) = q :=
  (h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective h).apply_symm_apply q

/-- Applying the inverse of `h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective` to `evalGen M x` recovers `x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective_symm_evalGen (h : Function.Surjective (evalGen.{u} M))
    (x : H1 zHat.{u} M) : (h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective h).symm (evalGen.{u} M x) = x :=
  (h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective h).symm_apply_apply x

end Injectivity

end Evaluation

section Discrete

variable {M : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [TopologicalSpace M] [DiscreteTopology M]
  [DistribMulAction zHat.{u} M] [ContinuousSMul zHat.{u} M]

/-- **Every element of a discrete continuous `zHat`-module is fixed by some congruence subgroup
`modSubgroup d`.** -/
theorem exists_modSubgroup_smul_eq_self (m : M) :
    ∃ d : ℕ+, ∀ x : zHat.{u}, x ∈ modSubgroup d → x • m = m := by
  obtain ⟨U, hU⟩ := exists_openNormalSubgroup_smul_eq_self (G := zHat.{u}) m
  obtain ⟨d, ψ, hψ⟩ := exists_monoidHom_mk_eq_toZMod U
  refine ⟨d, fun x hx ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [mem_modSubgroup] at hx
  have hmk : (x : zHat.{u} ⧸ U.toSubgroup) = 1 := by
    simpa [hx] using hψ (Additive.ofMul x)
  exact hU x ((QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff x).mp hmk)

omit [TopologicalSpace M] [DiscreteTopology M] [ContinuousSMul zHat.{u} M] in
/-- The partial geometric sum `∑ j < n, zHat.gen ^ j • m`. -/
private def geomSum (m : M) (n : ℕ) : M :=
  ∑ j ∈ Finset.range n, (gen : zHat.{u}) ^ j • m

omit [TopologicalSpace M] [DiscreteTopology M] [ContinuousSMul zHat.{u} M] in
private theorem geomSum_add (m : M) (a b : ℕ) :
    geomSum.{u} m (a + b) = geomSum.{u} m a + (gen : zHat.{u}) ^ a • geomSum.{u} m b := by
  dsimp only [geomSum]
  rw [Finset.sum_range_add, Finset.smul_sum]
  congr 1
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ ↦ by rw [pow_add, mul_smul]

omit [TopologicalSpace M] [DiscreteTopology M] [ContinuousSMul zHat.{u} M] in
private theorem genSubId_geomSum (m : M) (n : ℕ) :
    genSubId.{u} M (geomSum.{u} m n) = (gen : zHat.{u}) ^ n • m - m := by
  rw [genSubId_apply, geomSum, Finset.smul_sum, ← Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
  have hterm : ∀ j : ℕ, gen • ((gen : zHat.{u}) ^ j • m) - (gen : zHat.{u}) ^ j • m =
      (gen : zHat.{u}) ^ (j + 1) • m - (gen : zHat.{u}) ^ j • m := fun j ↦ by
    rw [pow_succ', mul_smul]
  simp_rw [hterm]
  rw [Finset.sum_range_sub (fun j ↦ (gen : zHat.{u}) ^ j • m) n, pow_zero, one_smul]

/-- Adjusting `x : zHat` by the `ZMod k`-representative power of `zHat.gen` lands in
`modSubgroup k`. -/
private theorem inv_gen_pow_mul_mem_modSubgroup (k : ℕ+) (x : zHat.{u}) :
    ((gen : zHat.{u}) ^ (toZMod k (Additive.ofMul x)).val)⁻¹ * x ∈ modSubgroup k := by
  rw [mem_modSubgroup, ofMul_mul, ofMul_inv, map_add, map_neg]
  have hga : toZMod k (Additive.ofMul ((gen : zHat.{u}) ^ (toZMod k (Additive.ofMul x)).val)) =
      ((toZMod k (Additive.ofMul x)).val : ZMod k) := by
    simp [nsmul_eq_mul]
  rw [hga, ZMod.natCast_zmod_val, neg_add_cancel]

/-- **Every augmentation generator `g • m - m` lies in `(zHat.gen - 1) M`** for a discrete
continuous `zHat`-module `M`. -/
theorem smul_sub_mem_range_genSubId (g : zHat.{u}) (m : M) :
    g • m - m ∈ (genSubId.{u} M).range := by
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := exists_modSubgroup_smul_eq_self.{u} m
  set a := (toZMod d (Additive.ofMul g)).val
  have hg : g • m = (gen : zHat.{u}) ^ a • m := by
    conv_lhs => rw [← mul_inv_cancel_left ((gen : zHat.{u}) ^ a) g]
    rw [mul_smul, hd _ (inv_gen_pow_mul_mem_modSubgroup d g)]
  exact ⟨geomSum.{u} m a, (genSubId_geomSum m a).trans (by rw [hg])⟩

variable (M) in
/-- **Presentation of the augmentation subgroup of a discrete continuous `zHat`-module.** The range
of `zHat.gen - 1` equals the subgroup generated by all `g • m - m` (`g ∈ zHat`, `m ∈ M`), so
`M ⧸ (zHat.gen - 1) M` is the `zHat`-coinvariants of `M`. -/
theorem range_genSubId_eq_closure_smul_sub :
    (genSubId.{u} M).range =
      AddSubgroup.closure {x : M | ∃ (g : zHat.{u}) (m : M), g • m - m = x} := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rintro _ ⟨m, rfl⟩
    exact AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨gen, m, rfl⟩
  · rw [AddSubgroup.closure_le]
    rintro _ ⟨g, m, rfl⟩
    exact smul_sub_mem_range_genSubId g m

variable (M) in
/-- **The `zHat`-coinvariants `M_{zHat}` of a discrete continuous `zHat`-module `M`**, presented as
the cokernel `M ⧸ (zHat.gen - 1) M`. By `TauCeti.zHat.range_genSubId_eq_closure_smul_sub`,
`(zHat.gen - 1) M` is the full `zHat`-augmentation subgroup of `M`. -/
abbrev Coinvariants : Type v :=
  M ⧸ (genSubId.{u} M).range

/-- In the `zHat`-coinvariants of a discrete continuous `zHat`-module, `zHat` acts trivially. -/
@[simp]
theorem mk_smul_eq_mk_coinvariants (g : zHat.{u}) (m : M) :
    (QuotientAddGroup.mk (g • m) : Coinvariants.{u} M) = QuotientAddGroup.mk m :=
  QuotientAddGroup.eq.mpr <| by
    simpa [sub_eq_add_neg, add_comm] using neg_mem (smul_sub_mem_range_genSubId g m)

omit [TopologicalSpace M] [DiscreteTopology M] [ContinuousSMul zHat.{u} M] in
/-- Partial geometric sums `geomSum m n` are periodic of period `r * d` when `gen ^ d` fixes `m`
and `r • m = 0`. -/
private theorem geomSum_mod_eq {m : M} {d r : ℕ} (hd : (gen : zHat.{u}) ^ d • m = m)
    (hr : r • m = 0) (n : ℕ) :
    geomSum.{u} m (n % (r * d)) = geomSum.{u} m n := by
  have hmul : ∀ t : ℕ, geomSum.{u} m (t * d) = t • geomSum.{u} m d := by
    intro t
    induction t with
    | zero => simp [geomSum]
    | succ t ih =>
      have hpow : (gen : zHat.{u}) ^ (t * d) • m = m := by
        rw [mul_comm, pow_mul]
        exact Subgroup.pow_mem (K := MulAction.stabilizer zHat.{u} m) hd t
      have hpow_sum : (gen : zHat.{u}) ^ (t * d) • geomSum.{u} m d = geomSum.{u} m d := by
        rw [geomSum, Finset.smul_sum]
        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ ↦ ?_
        rw [← mul_smul, ← pow_add, add_comm, pow_add, mul_smul, hpow]
      rw [Nat.succ_mul, geomSum_add, ih, hpow_sum, succ_nsmul]
  have hSk : geomSum.{u} m (r * d) = 0 := by
    rw [hmul r, geomSum, Finset.smul_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun j _ ↦ ?_
    rw [smul_comm, hr, smul_zero]
  have hper : ∀ a q : ℕ, geomSum.{u} m (a + r * d * q) = geomSum.{u} m a := by
    intro a q
    induction q with
    | zero => simp
    | succ q ih =>
      rw [mul_add, mul_one, ← add_assoc, geomSum_add, hSk, smul_zero, add_zero, ih]
  conv_rhs => rw [← Nat.mod_add_div n (r * d)]
  exact (hper (n % (r * d)) (n / (r * d))).symm

omit [TopologicalSpace M] [DiscreteTopology M] [ContinuousSMul zHat.{u} M] in
/-- Evaluating `geomSum m` on representatives in `ZMod k` yields a `1`-cocycle whenever
`modSubgroup k` fixes `m` and `geomSum m` has period `k`. -/
private theorem isCocycle₁_geomSum_toZMod {m : M} {k : ℕ+}
    (hmodk : ∀ x : zHat.{u}, x ∈ modSubgroup k → x • m = m)
    (hSmod : ∀ n : ℕ, geomSum.{u} m (n % (k : ℕ)) = geomSum.{u} m n) :
    IsCocycle₁ (fun x : zHat.{u} ↦ geomSum.{u} m (toZMod k (Additive.ofMul x)).val) := by
  have hfixS : ∀ (u₀ : zHat.{u}), u₀ ∈ modSubgroup k → ∀ n : ℕ,
      u₀ • geomSum.{u} m n = geomSum.{u} m n := by
    intro u₀ hu₀ n
    rw [geomSum, Finset.smul_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ ↦ ?_
    rw [← mul_smul, mul_comm u₀, mul_smul, hmodk u₀ hu₀]
  intro x y
  dsimp only
  set a := (toZMod k (Additive.ofMul x)).val
  set b := (toZMod k (Additive.ofMul y)).val
  have hxy : (toZMod k (Additive.ofMul (x * y))).val = (a + b) % (k : ℕ) := by
    have hcast : toZMod k (Additive.ofMul (x * y)) = ((a + b : ℕ) : ZMod k) := by
      rw [ofMul_mul, map_add, Nat.cast_add, ZMod.natCast_zmod_val, ZMod.natCast_zmod_val]
    rw [hcast, ZMod.val_natCast]
  have hxS : x • geomSum.{u} m b = (gen : zHat.{u}) ^ a • geomSum.{u} m b := by
    conv_lhs => rw [← mul_inv_cancel_left (gen ^ a) x]
    rw [mul_smul, hfixS _ (inv_gen_pow_mul_mem_modSubgroup k x) b]
  rw [hxy, hSmod (a + b), geomSum_add, ← hxS, add_comm]

/-- **Every torsion element of a discrete continuous `zHat`-module is the value at `zHat.gen` of a
continuous `1`-cocycle.** -/
theorem exists_apply_gen_eq_of_isOfFinAddOrder {m : M} (hm : IsOfFinAddOrder m) :
    ∃ f : Z1 zHat.{u} M, f.val gen = m := by
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := exists_modSubgroup_smul_eq_self.{u} m
  let r : ℕ+ := ⟨addOrderOf m, hm.addOrderOf_pos⟩
  let k : ℕ+ := r * d
  have hmodk : ∀ x : zHat.{u}, x ∈ modSubgroup k → x • m = m := by
    intro x hx
    apply hd x
    rw [mem_modSubgroup] at hx ⊢
    have hdvd : (d : ℕ) ∣ (k : ℕ) := PNat.mul_coe r d ▸ dvd_mul_left (d : ℕ) r
    rw [← cast_toZMod hdvd, hx, ZMod.cast_zero]
  have hgend : (gen : zHat.{u}) ^ (d : ℕ) • m = m :=
    hd _ (by rw [mem_modSubgroup]; simp)
  have hSmod : ∀ n : ℕ, geomSum.{u} m (n % (k : ℕ)) = geomSum.{u} m n :=
    geomSum_mod_eq hgend (addOrderOf_nsmul_eq_zero m)
  have hc_cont : Continuous (fun x : zHat.{u} ↦
      geomSum.{u} m (toZMod k (Additive.ofMul x)).val) :=
    (continuous_of_discreteTopology : Continuous fun z : ZMod k ↦ geomSum.{u} m z.val).comp
      ((continuous_toZMod k).comp continuous_ofMul)
  refine ⟨⟨_, mem_Z1_iff.mpr ⟨hc_cont, isCocycle₁_geomSum_toZMod hmodk hSmod⟩⟩, ?_⟩
  have hgen1 : (toZMod k (Additive.ofMul (gen : zHat.{u}))).val = 1 % (k : ℕ) := by
    have h1 : toZMod k (Additive.ofMul (gen : zHat.{u})) = ((1 : ℕ) : ZMod k) := by simp
    rw [h1, ZMod.val_natCast]
  dsimp only
  rw [hgen1, hSmod 1]
  simp [geomSum]

variable (M) in
/-- **Evaluation at `zHat.gen` is surjective on `H¹(zHat, M)`** for every discrete torsion
continuous `zHat`-module `M`. -/
theorem evalGen_surjective (hM : IsAddTorsion M) :
    Function.Surjective (evalGen.{u} M) :=
  evalGen_surjective_of_forall_exists fun m ↦ exists_apply_gen_eq_of_isOfFinAddOrder.{u} (hM m)

variable (M) in
/-- **First continuous cohomology of `zHat` with coefficients in a discrete torsion module is its
coinvariant quotient**: `H¹(zHat, M) ≃+ zHat.Coinvariants M` via evaluation at `zHat.gen`. -/
def h1AddEquivCoinvariants (hM : IsAddTorsion M) :
    H1 zHat.{u} M ≃+ Coinvariants.{u} M :=
  h1AddEquivCoinvariantsOfSurjective (evalGen_surjective M hM)

/-- `h1AddEquivCoinvariants` acts as `evalGen`. -/
@[simp]
theorem h1AddEquivCoinvariants_apply (hM : IsAddTorsion M) (x : H1 zHat.{u} M) :
    h1AddEquivCoinvariants.{u} M hM x = evalGen.{u} M x :=
  (rfl)

/-- The underlying additive homomorphism of `h1AddEquivCoinvariants` is `evalGen`. -/
@[simp]
theorem h1AddEquivCoinvariants_toAddMonoidHom (hM : IsAddTorsion M) :
    (h1AddEquivCoinvariants.{u} M hM : H1 zHat.{u} M →+ Coinvariants.{u} M) = evalGen.{u} M :=
  (rfl)

/-- Evaluating at `zHat.gen` cancels the inverse of `h1AddEquivCoinvariants`. -/
@[simp]
theorem evalGen_h1AddEquivCoinvariants_symm (hM : IsAddTorsion M) (q : Coinvariants.{u} M) :
    evalGen.{u} M ((h1AddEquivCoinvariants.{u} M hM).symm q) = q :=
  (h1AddEquivCoinvariants.{u} M hM).apply_symm_apply q

/-- Applying the inverse of `h1AddEquivCoinvariants` to `evalGen M x` recovers `x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem h1AddEquivCoinvariants_symm_evalGen (hM : IsAddTorsion M) (x : H1 zHat.{u} M) :
    (h1AddEquivCoinvariants.{u} M hM).symm (evalGen.{u} M x) = x :=
  (h1AddEquivCoinvariants.{u} M hM).symm_apply_apply x

variable (M) in
/-- **For a finite discrete continuous `zHat`-module `M`, `#H¹(zHat, M) = #H⁰(zHat, M)`.** -/
theorem natCard_H1_eq_natCard_H0 [Finite M] :
    Nat.card (H1 zHat.{u} M) = Nat.card (H0 zHat.{u} M) :=
  (Nat.card_congr (h1AddEquivCoinvariants.{u} M isAddTorsion_of_finite).toEquiv).trans
    (natCard_coinvariants_eq_natCard_H0 M)

variable (M) in
/-- **A finite discrete continuous `zHat`-module with trivial invariants has vanishing `H¹`.** -/
theorem subsingleton_H1_of_subsingleton_H0 [Finite M] [Subsingleton (H0 zHat.{u} M)] :
    Subsingleton (H1 zHat.{u} M) := by
  have hcard : Nat.card (H1 zHat.{u} M) = 1 :=
    (natCard_H1_eq_natCard_H0.{u} M).trans (Nat.card_unique (α := H0 zHat.{u} M))
  exact Nat.card_eq_one_iff_unique.mp hcard |>.1

end Discrete

